# wp-next-bagels stack

- **Router**: Next.js **App Router** (`app/`). Route Handlers live under `app/api/**/route.ts`.
- **Languages**: `.js`, `.jsx`, and `.tsx` coexist. Match the extension and typing style of the file you edit; prefer TypeScript for **new** files only when neighboring code is already TS.
- **Page shell** (most routes): `Header` → `Container`. Import from `components/Header`, `components/Container`. Root chrome (`html`/`body`, global styles, footer) is in `app/layout.tsx`.
- **SEO / titles**: Export `metadata` or `generateMetadata` from each `page.tsx`. Use `CMS_NAME` from `lib/constants.js`. Emoji in titles (e.g. 🥯) matches existing pages.
- **Imports**: Use relative paths into `lib/`, `utils/`, `config/`, `components/` (e.g. `../../lib/api`).
- **Global client state**: `little-state-machine` is configured in `app/providers.tsx`; extend the store shape there only when adding persisted UI/order fields.
- **Styling**: Tailwind utility classes; optional colocated `*.module.css` per component.

```tsx
// Typical page (Server Component) + metadata
export const metadata = { title: `${CMS_NAME} …`, description: `${CMS_NAME} …` };

export default async function Page() {
  const { navItems } = await getNavItems(false);
  return (
    <>
      <Header navItems={navItems} />
      <Container>{/* content */}</Container>
    </>
  );
}
```
